            <profile id="dd39-6b2f-c4c1-60f8" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and light armour. May have buckler (+1 pt), shield (+2 pts), either javelins (+2 pts) or bow (+3 pts), and either thrusting or throwing spear (+2 pts). May ride a horse (+8 pts). One Voevodo may be upgraded to Slav Army Standard Bearer (+15 pts). Mounted Slav characters have Feigned Flight. Early Balkan Slav armies: only one Voevodo may be chosen from the Commander entries, and he must be upgraded to Grand Zhapan (+25 pts) who counts as the Army General. Later Balkan Slav armies: one Voevodo may be upgraded to Knyaz (Prince) who counts as Army General (+25 pts). (Byzantium p.75)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="5c25-85e4-c03b-3e7c" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024" value="5+ with Buckler +1 in hand-to-hand only">
