            </profile>
            <profile id="6d0a-55e7-6d4a-2b14" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon and light armour. May have buckler (+1 pt), shield (+2 pts), either javelins (+2 pts) or bow (+3 pts), and either thrusting or throwing spear (+2 pts). May ride a horse (+8 pts). Mounted Slav characters have Feigned Flight. In Early Balkan Slav armies only one Voevodo may be chosen from the Commander entries (Zhupans are not restricted). (Byzantium p.75)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="b2f5-2355-cbd4-22c3" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
