  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="5c9f-b8e4-7840-a77d" name="Bulgars &amp; Slavs (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>BULGARS &amp; SLAVS (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.72-75): Early &amp; Later Balkan Bulgar and Slav armies, 643-1018 AD. Special rules: Balkan Ruse - Bulgars and Slavs may always place D3 patches of difficult terrain (about 6" by 6") in their deployment zone before deployment begins. Bulgar and Slav infantry are Warband, Light Infantry with Stealth.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Bulgars &amp; Slavs - Early Balkan Slavs]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  EARLY BALKAN SLAVS. Characters up to 33%; Infantry at least 33%; Cavalry up to 33% (one unit of Slav Nobles may be chosen). Special rule: only one Voevodo may be chosen from the Commander entries, and he must be upgraded to Grand Zhapan (+25 pts) who counts as the Army General.
[Bulgars &amp; Slavs - Later Balkan Slavs]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  LATER BALKAN SLAVS. Characters up to 33%; Infantry at least 25% (Slav Brigands may not be chosen); Cavalry up to 50%. Special rule: one Voevodo may be upgraded to Knyaz (Prince) who counts as Army General (+25 pts).
[Bulgars &amp; Slavs - Early Balkan Bulgars]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  EARLY BALKAN BULGARS. Characters up to 33%; Infantry at least 25%, up to 33% of the points may be spent on Slav infantry (not enforced); Cavalry any amount, up to 25% of the points may be spent on Slav cavalry (not enforced; Slav Nobles may not be chosen). Special rules: if Nobles are chosen, at least two units of Horse Archers or Elite Horse Archers must be taken as well. If no other Army General is chosen, a Tarkan may be upgraded to Kavkan (+25 pts), who counts as Army General.
[Bulgars &amp; Slavs - Later Balkan Bulgars]
  Characters: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 25%
  Cavalry: up to 33%
  LATER BALKAN BULGARS. Characters up to 33%; Infantry at least 25%, up to 33% of the points may be spent on Slav infantry (not enforced); Cavalry up to 33%, up to 25% of the points on Slav cavalry (not enforced; Slav Nobles may not be chosen). Special rules: Bulgar Foot Warriors are not subject to Warband Psychology Rule 2 and Rule 3. Any unit of Bulgar Foot Warriors may be upgraded to Later Warriors (+1 pt, Leadership 5). Warriors may deploy behind a Palisade Fence (up to 18" at 4 pts per inch, Balkan Ruse rule 2; documented only; requires at least 33% of the points spent on Warriors or Later Warriors).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
